export anchor DimModeStyle:
    number: 228
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Dim mode
    idea: A soft low-contrast slate around #22272e for long sessions, with muted colours, generous line height and one reading column that groups projects by what needs attention, while every text pair still passes AA.
    base: dark
    palette:
        dim: #22272e, the page, the header and the style sheet
        panel: #2b3139, project groups, the chart box, summary chips and fields
        raised: #343b44, the current nav item, the secondary button and the avatar
        line: #444c56, every border and divider and the meter tracks
        text: #c9d1d9, body and names, held well below white
        muted: #9aa5b1, labels, meta and axis text
        blue: #7ea9dc, links, meters, this week bars and focus
        button: #41618a, the primary button fill, a muted blue
        onButton: #e6edf5, text on the primary button
        lastWeek: #7d8794, last week bars
        ok: #8fc49c, the On track word and icon
        risk: #d8b46c, the At risk word and icon
        bad: #e3958c, the Behind word and icon and the overdue line
    type:
        One stack, -apple-system, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Noto Sans.
        Base 15px at 1.65. The greeting is 26px at 500, the lede 17px,
        section titles 15px at 600, group labels 13px at 500 and meta 13px.
        Nothing is bold beyond 600.
    layout:
        A 200px sidebar ruled on the right holds a small blue dot with the
        name and six text-only nav links, Home on a raised tile. The header
        bar holds search, a muted blue New project button, a quiet bell and
        Mara Okafor. The content is one 760px reading column. It starts
        with the date and Good morning, Mara, then a lede where a clock and
        4 tasks are overdue sit in soft red, followed by Start there, then
        the rest of the week. The four figures follow as small inline chips
        with the number in bold, the overdue chip red. Projects by status
        then shows three groups in order, Behind, At risk and On track, each
        labelled with its status and a count, and each a bordered panel of
        rows with name, category, a thin blue meter with percent, due date
        and tasks. Tasks completed is a bordered chart box with a caption
        naming the totals and colours. Recent activity is a ruled list with
        times on the right. Below 760px the sidebar becomes a scrolling row
        and search moves to its own row.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 12px row padding, 48px between sections, a 760px column with 32px sides.
    density: Low. One column, with projects grouped into Behind, At risk and On track.
    corners: 6px on panels, fields, buttons and chips. Round avatar.
    borders: 1px #444c56 around panels and between rows. No heavier rules.
    shadows: None. Low glare matters more than depth.
    icons:
        Line icons at 1.6 stroke, 17px, only where they carry meaning.
        Status is a check circle, a triangle or a crossed square with the
        word, also used as the group heading.
    focus: A 2px soft blue outline offset 2px.
    tone: Calm and guiding, such as 4 tasks are overdue. Start there, then the rest of the week.
